We were recently in Copenhagen, and visited Vor Frelsers Kirke (Church of Our Savior), mainly to access the views of the city from the famous bell tower.  While the rest of the family did the (terrifying)  spiral exterior climb, I stayed on the inside portion, where a CARILLON was on display. I believe it is still functional, and is amongst the largest in Europe. 

